(5238706, 759107, 67152, '<td valign="top">Jan<br/>I think you did a nice job of setting the image up.  The ''keystoning'' effect does work nicely, and I think the image carries the theme of silence to MOST viewers.  <br/> <br/>However, there appears to be some significant issues with the ''starbursts'' from the lights above, the overall appearance of the details of the walls and pews and all are somewhat missing.  These issues are likely due to the camera/ glass you are using.  I have noticed very similar effects in my Panasonic Lumix camera.  It takes a decent shot in really good light, but does not really deliver when inside (even if on a tripod).  I think this is one reason why you ended up with some low score.  I would have given this about a 6 if I voted.<br/> <br/><i>Additional comment:  I guess I should have looked at the camera you shot with more closely - I assumed you were using a very similar one to my Lumix P&amp;S.  I have seen issues with the starbursts in that camera and was trying only to provide a bit of comparison.  My bad...</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-02-04 08:23:27.</i></td>', 'JanI think you did a nice job of setting the image up.  The ''keystoning'' effect does work nicely, and I think the image carries the theme of silence to MOST viewers.   However, there appears to be some significant issues with the ''starbursts'' from the lights above, the overall appearance of the details of the walls and pews and all are somewhat missing.  These issues are likely due to the camera/ glass you are using.  I have noticed very similar effects in my Panasonic Lumix camera.  It takes a decent shot in really good light, but does not really deliver when inside (even if on a tripod).  I think this is one reason why you ended up with some low score.  I would have given this about a 6 if I voted. Additional comment:  I guess I should have looked at the camera you shot with more closely - I assumed you were using a very similar one to my Lumix P&S.  I have seen issues with the starbursts in that camera and was trying only to provide a bit of comparison.  My bad...', '2009-02-04 07:53:15.000000', '2009-02-04 08:23:27.000000', 0),
