(5239770, 759161, 83080, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a very effective shot.  I was hopping to see this on the front page or at least in the top ten, so I''m a little shocked to see it here in the 5 range.  I know there were other finger to lips shots, but this one really stands out compositionally imho and I''m a little disappointed DPCers didn''t score it better.</td>', 'Congratulations on a very effective shot.  I was hopping to see this on the front page or at least in the top ten, so I''m a little shocked to see it here in the 5 range.  I know there were other finger to lips shots, but this one really stands out compositionally imho and I''m a little disappointed DPCers didn''t score it better.', '2009-02-04 19:07:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5239777, 759640, 83080, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your first challenge.  Great combination of simplicity and imagination in this shot and I look forward to seeing what you come up with in the future.</td>', 'Congratulations on your first challenge.  Great combination of simplicity and imagination in this shot and I look forward to seeing what you come up with in the future.', '2009-02-04 19:11:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5239797, 760294, 30807, '<td valign="top">Oh, my! I think Heavenly Father knew you needed just the right weather, and here it is!<br/> <br/>I have seen professionally taken shots from explorers which were not as good as this - what wonderful scenery!  I am a bit surprised that you got such a shot on an ixus - I must revise my opinions!<br/> <br/>Very lovely shot - you must have laboured hard to get to this point, but it was well worth it. <br/> <br/>I would love to see others from the days photos, if there is any chance!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oh, my! I think Heavenly Father knew you needed just the right weather, and here it is! I have seen professionally taken shots from explorers which were not as good as this - what wonderful scenery!  I am a bit surprised that you got such a shot on an ixus - I must revise my opinions! Very lovely shot - you must have laboured hard to get to this point, but it was well worth it.  I would love to see others from the days photos, if there is any chance! ', '2009-02-04 19:25:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5239810, 760451, 30807, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot - I immediately pictured it with a white kitten trying to catch falling feathers - now there would be another lovely shot too - you have captured a lovely range of gentle tones from near white to mid/darker gray, and how delightful an image -very well done</td>', 'Beautiful shot - I immediately pictured it with a white kitten trying to catch falling feathers - now there would be another lovely shot too - you have captured a lovely range of gentle tones from near white to mid/darker gray, and how delightful an image -very well done', '2009-02-04 19:29:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5239821, 759175, 51841, '<td valign="top">Barely made it into the Top 100, but for my fist submission, I''m satisfied. Thanks for the comments and the votes. I think it would have been better if you could see what''s written on the tape, of course, but I''m pleased anyways.</td>', 'Barely made it into the Top 100, but for my fist submission, I''m satisfied. Thanks for the comments and the votes. I think it would have been better if you could see what''s written on the tape, of course, but I''m pleased anyways.', '2009-02-04 19:35:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5239824, 760325, 83080, '<td valign="top">A bit under rated imho.  Despite my suggestions below I gave this an 8 for the magnificently eerie haunting feel you created with the IR.  The <a href="//en.wikisource.org/wiki/Sunday_morning" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Stevens poem</a> is awesome and now I''m inspired to read some of his other works.  Thanks!<br/></td>', 'A bit under rated imho.  Despite my suggestions below I gave this an 8 for the magnificently eerie haunting feel you created with the IR.  The Stevens poem is awesome and now I''m inspired to read some of his other works.  Thanks!', '2009-02-04 19:37:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5239830, 760435, 83080, '<td valign="top">WAY under rated imho!  It looks like you got judged based on how many people had similar ideas rather than how well you created and executed this version (in a half hour lol).</td>', 'WAY under rated imho!  It looks like you got judged based on how many people had similar ideas rather than how well you created and executed this version (in a half hour lol).', '2009-02-04 19:41:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5239852, 759832, 100393, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i>  Why, oh why, did you not clone out that speck on the nose????   </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That wouldn''t be allowed under basic would it??</td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera:  Why, oh why, did you not clone out that speck on the nose????     That wouldn''t be allowed under basic would it??', '2009-02-04 20:00:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5239929, 759709, 90414, '<td valign="top">Lovely photo that worked (for me, anyway) both in B/W and for the challenge. Some voters need to be smacked between the eyes by the challenge topic... others are more open-minded. Sorry this missed the top 10, but congrats on a wonderful image!</td>', 'Lovely photo that worked (for me, anyway) both in B/W and for the challenge. Some voters need to be smacked between the eyes by the challenge topic... others are more open-minded. Sorry this missed the top 10, but congrats on a wonderful image!', '2009-02-04 20:51:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5239978, 760115, 68947, '<td valign="top">Well...<br/> <br/>The twigs in the ground distract me.  The bench distracts me.  I know they must have been horribly noisy, walking on that snow.  The shadows or footprints in the background take my eyes away from the ducks. It''s too messy a shot.  Too bad you couldn''t have cut the bolts off the bottom of the bench...they distract me.  Looks over processed.  I wish the ducks had have been facing us.  They''re not symetrical.  The footprints beside them distract me.  There''s a bit of a tilt to the bench...woulda been better if had have been level.  They should have all had their heads going in the same direction...too bad you couldn''t have trained them.<br/> <br/>IMHO..........  <br/> <br/>just doesn''t do it for me.<br/> <br/>:P<br/> <br/>Ahhhhh......got that out of my system LOL!!!!<br/> <br/>Cute shot, Mich! <br/>XO<br/> <br/></td>', 'Well... The twigs in the ground distract me.  The bench distracts me.  I know they must have been horribly noisy, walking on that snow.  The shadows or footprints in the background take my eyes away from the ducks. It''s too messy a shot.  Too bad you couldn''t have cut the bolts off the bottom of the bench...they distract me.  Looks over processed.  I wish the ducks had have been facing us.  They''re not symetrical.  The footprints beside them distract me.  There''s a bit of a tilt to the bench...woulda been better if had have been level.  They should have all had their heads going in the same direction...too bad you couldn''t have trained them. IMHO..........   just doesn''t do it for me. :P Ahhhhh......got that out of my system LOL!!!! Cute shot, Mich! XO ', '2009-02-04 21:25:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5240131, 760294, 80096, '<td valign="top">Beautiful. Well worth the blue.</td>', 'Beautiful. Well worth the blue.', '2009-02-04 23:58:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5240204, 760115, 54645, '<td valign="top">Are they looking for their buddy with the broken wing? <br/> <br/>Something very interesting about the presence of the bench. I''m not sure why, but it''s intriguing.<br/> <br/>ETA: Is she joking? I just read her comment...I assume it has something to do with her nit pick thread. Ok, I''m sure she is joking.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-02-05 00:54:31.</i></td>', 'Are they looking for their buddy with the broken wing?  Something very interesting about the presence of the bench. I''m not sure why, but it''s intriguing. ETA: Is she joking? I just read her comment...I assume it has something to do with her nit pick thread. Ok, I''m sure she is joking.', '2009-02-05 00:52:39.000000', '2009-02-05 00:54:31.000000', 0),
(5240438, 760395, 63269, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by briantammy:</b></div><hr/><i> this is why i''m pretty much giving up around here.  this should''ve scored so much higher.  i gave you a 7. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Aw, don''t give up... I think I really enjoy entering challenges just for the comments. And then comments like yours make up for all the negative ones I personally don''t quite understand. ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by briantammy: this is why i''m pretty much giving up around here.  this should''ve scored so much higher.  i gave you a 7.   Aw, don''t give up... I think I really enjoy entering challenges just for the comments. And then comments like yours make up for all the negative ones I personally don''t quite understand. ;)', '2009-02-05 07:17:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5240726, 760218, 78303, '<td valign="top">I just play around and have fun with my photos.  Then, when I see one like this, it makes me appreciate it all the more.  You did an excellent job.  Very nice artwork.</td>', 'I just play around and have fun with my photos.  Then, when I see one like this, it makes me appreciate it all the more.  You did an excellent job.  Very nice artwork.', '2009-02-05 12:09:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5240728, 760294, 78303, '<td valign="top">You have done two things for me here.  One, the picture is excellent.  Very well done.  Secondly, I did not realize the extent of the climate variances in Iran.  I need to work on my world geography more.  Thank you for posting.</td>', 'You have done two things for me here.  One, the picture is excellent.  Very well done.  Secondly, I did not realize the extent of the climate variances in Iran.  I need to work on my world geography more.  Thank you for posting.', '2009-02-05 12:10:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5240743, 760124, 101849, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JMart:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kevip6:</b></div><hr/><i> This was one of my top two, I really don''t get the results in this challenge. This is a great shot that fits the challenge better then most others and is technically excellent. You (and many others in this chanenge) were robbed! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I agree.  I was expecting to see this on the front page today and am a little disappointed with DPCers for giving this a sub 6 score.  Hope you''ll keep your awesome out of the box creativity going in the future.<br/> <br/>ETA:<br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by benfica:</b></div><hr/><i> I was going for a sci-fi silence. I guess not everyone got it. thank you all for the comments </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes, it gave me the feel of a trial on planet Crypton right away :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks JMart for the one up. Nah the scoring wont keep me down. And yes im def going for the creative angle. I like going outside of the box with these challanges. It gets a little boring to see 20 different versions of the same picture. Watch the apple challange if i get my macro lense in time i have something special planned for that one.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-02-05 12:20:49.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by JMart: Originally posted by kevip6: This was one of my top two, I really don''t get the results in this challenge. This is a great shot that fits the challenge better then most others and is technically excellent. You (and many others in this chanenge) were robbed!  I agree.  I was expecting to see this on the front page today and am a little disappointed with DPCers for giving this a sub 6 score.  Hope you''ll keep your awesome out of the box creativity going in the future. ETA:Originally posted by benfica: I was going for a sci-fi silence. I guess not everyone got it. thank you all for the comments  Yes, it gave me the feel of a trial on planet Crypton right away :)   Thanks JMart for the one up. Nah the scoring wont keep me down. And yes im def going for the creative angle. I like going outside of the box with these challanges. It gets a little boring to see 20 different versions of the same picture. Watch the apple challange if i get my macro lense in time i have something special planned for that one.', '2009-02-05 12:20:01.000000', '2009-02-05 12:20:49.000000', 0),
(5240879, 760395, 23484, '<td valign="top">This should have scored higher than a 4.3 without a doubt.  I think the title is perfect for the challenge.</td>', 'This should have scored higher than a 4.3 without a doubt.  I think the title is perfect for the challenge.', '2009-02-05 13:06:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5240906, 760395, 61961, '<td valign="top">You got killed by the number of similarly themed entries, and your photo lacks that count-the-pores sharpness that is <i>de rigeur</i> for dpc.  Personally I don''t like your choice of frame, but the photo itself is very appealing.  The brutal crop, somewhat awkward stance, "stiff neck", and partially-seen mouth all add interest for me.  I also very much like the color palette.</td>', 'You got killed by the number of similarly themed entries, and your photo lacks that count-the-pores sharpness that is de rigeur for dpc.  Personally I don''t like your choice of frame, but the photo itself is very appealing.  The brutal crop, somewhat awkward stance, "stiff neck", and partially-seen mouth all add interest for me.  I also very much like the color palette.', '2009-02-05 13:26:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5240983, 759107, 67697, '<td valign="top">Jan, I gave this a 6 and I''ll see if I can find the right words to explain what would make me score this higher.  I totally think that there is nothing more peaceful and quiet than to walk in to a big beautiful church when no one else is present.  And I look at this photo and I can see the scene you have captured.  BUT I guess for me to give this higher than a 6 I had to feel the "mood" of the moment.  I think for a place like this, the mood is best created by lighting.  For me the top half was too bright, and the ceiling lights almost felt like an interruption in the setting.  I''d want to see a softer glow coming from the windows and from those hanging lights.  This then allows one''s attention to focus on the highlight of the church, which is the altar.  What if you maybe decreased the f-stop some more, maybe f 11? And increased the shutter speed a smidge?  If my thinking here needs more explanation, just send a PM :)</td>', 'Jan, I gave this a 6 and I''ll see if I can find the right words to explain what would make me score this higher.  I totally think that there is nothing more peaceful and quiet than to walk in to a big beautiful church when no one else is present.  And I look at this photo and I can see the scene you have captured.  BUT I guess for me to give this higher than a 6 I had to feel the "mood" of the moment.  I think for a place like this, the mood is best created by lighting.  For me the top half was too bright, and the ceiling lights almost felt like an interruption in the setting.  I''d want to see a softer glow coming from the windows and from those hanging lights.  This then allows one''s attention to focus on the highlight of the church, which is the altar.  What if you maybe decreased the f-stop some more, maybe f 11? And increased the shutter speed a smidge?  If my thinking here needs more explanation, just send a PM :)', '2009-02-05 14:18:00.000000', NULL, 0),
